# A UDP echo server on the board: the station connects to the network the board keeps (wlan set in the console), gets an
# address by DHCP and sends every UDP packet that comes to port 7777 back to its sender; each one is shown. From a PC in
# the same network: python udpecho.py <address of the board> (next to this file), or any program that sends UDP. It
# needs the WiFi package on the board (F9 in Asmonite writes it there); the program loads the WiFi from it itself
# (inc/wifi.abel): "run udpecho" in the console, or F9 in Asmonite.
#
# The ESP32-S3: the same program as abelle/examples/esp32/udpecho.abel of the ESP32; its text goes to the USB port of
# the chip (inc/usb.abel), the WiFi needs its package on the board (F9 writes it).
# It serves until Stop in the tab Serial of Asmonite (Ctrl+C); then the console is there again, its WiFi stays.
target "esp32s3"
include "inc/usb.abel"
include "inc/net.abel"

PORT = 7777
peer: char[4]                       # the sender of the last packet
text: char[64]                      # its first bytes as a text

def main():
    println("UDP echo (aBelle)")
    net_init()
    print("connecting to ")
    println(wifi_saved_name())
    r = wifi_connect_saved()
    if r != 0:
        print("wifi_connect: error ")
        print_int(r)
        print(" (")
        print(wifi_error_text(r))
        print(")")
        print(", status ")
        print_int(wifi_status())
        println("")
    elif not dhcp_run(): println("dhcp: no answer")
    else:
        print("listening on ")
        print_ip(net_ip)
        put_char(':')
        print_int(PORT)
        print("  (mask ")
        print_ip(net_mask)
        println(")")
        count = 0
        while True:
            n = net_recv(100)
            if n == 0 or udp_dport != PORT: continue
            count += 1
            copy(peer, rx + udp_from, 4)
            port = udp_sport
            copy(udp_payload(), rx + udp_off, n)
            k = n
            if k > 60: k = 60
            copy(text, rx + udp_off, k)
            text[k] = 0
            for i in 0..k:
                if text[i] < 32 or text[i] > 126: text[i] = '.'
            print("echo ")
            print_int(count)
            print(": ")
            print_int(n)
            print(" bytes from ")
            print_ip(peer)
            put_char(':')
            print_int(port)
            print(" ")
            println(text)
            r = udp_send(peer, PORT, port, n)
            if r != 0:
                print("udp_send: ")
                print_int(r)
                println("")
    println("udpecho end")
